      {
        "row" : 0,
        "col" : 0,
        "sizeX" : 0,
        "width" : 12,
        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "",
          "",
          "",
          "The spatial statistics above includes Moran's I value, which detects the presence of non-random spatial patterns in the data. Positive Moran's I indicates spatial depedence (observed values are influenced by nearby values), and negative  Moran's I indicates spatial heterogeniety (observed values are influenced by other regional factors).  Here we see positive Moran's I indivaring spatial dependence.",
          "",
          "In the presence of spatial dependence, Lagrange Multiplier (LM) tests are used to compare an OLS model to models including Spatial Lag or Spatial Error. LM tests return p-value (probability that the observed spatial pattern is random) and z-score (deviation of observed value from the mean in units of standard deviation). A \"significant p-value\" is one that is sufficiently small to allow rejection of randomness. A common threshold is 0.05, meaning 95% probability that the pattern is not random.",
          "",
          "To determine whether a spatial algotithm is prefered you may use the following logic:",
          "",
          "* If neither LM error or lag p-value is significant then the non-spatial OLS model is preferred.",
          "* If only one LM test has significant p-value then the associated spatial alogithm is preferred. ",
          "* If both LM tests have significant p-values then evaluate Robust LM tests: ",
          "* If only one Robust LM  model has a significant robust p-value then the associated spatial alogithm is preferred. ",
          "* If both Robust LM error and lag test p-values are significant then the model with a larger z-score is preferred.",
          " ",
          " ",
          " In the spatial statistics results above, observe that:",
          "",
          " * Positive Moran's I indicates spatial dependence. ",
          " * Both LM error and lag p-values are significant, so review the Robust LM tests.",
          " * Both Robust LM error and lag p-values are significant, so review Robust LM z-scores.",
          " * The Robust LM error z-score is larger than the Robust LM lag z-score.",
          " * Therefore, a Spatial Error regression model would be expected to provide the most reliable predictions.",
          "",
          "These and other spatial statistics are available for evaluation by experienced users using functions in the `oraclesai.metrics` module. For those without experience in evaluating these statistics, the `SpatialAdaptiveRegressor` automatically selects the preferred alogrithm."
        ],
